{"kind":"propose","text":"PROPOSAL: adopt the 2026-08-27 board-trust audit remediation direction, for hugh's ratification. Six principles, each with its first enforcement site: (1) The projection never names an actor in waiting_on without an admissible closing act (fold.go projectCommitments). (2) Reviewed-and-rejected implementation lanes have a defined, truthful closure when their repair child supersedes them; no lane is left permanently reported. (3) Staleness is recorded, not refused, at every write boundary, matching merge.md:122; only retirement refuses (admission.go refuseDeadBases). (4) Artifact succession is content-aware: a merge republishes only artifacts whose covered subtree actually changed (cmd/gs/succession.go planSuccession), ending path-coverage republish churn. (5) Refiles are machine-readable — a replacing request names its predecessor in a declared field, preferably via the guarded reassignment — so chains are visible on the board. (6) A merged lane's worktree is removed at merge completion; worktree hygiene is part of closure (AGENTS.md step 6 gains an enforcement point). Implementation requests 673659b8 (closure) and the staleness-policy filing already rest on the audit assert 1216de75; items 4-6 will be filed as requests after this proposal is ratified or amended. Measured stakes in the assert: 37.8 durable events per merged change and 40% of commitments closing empty."}